From: beryl7-travel
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: cancel the scan timeout of a removed BSS that is not the first

wpa_driver_nl80211_if_remove() cancels the scan timeout only when it removes the
driver's first BSS. A scan started by any other BSS keeps its timeout armed with
that BSS's ctx, which the caller frees right after; when the timeout fires and
aborting the scan fails, wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout() reports
EVENT_SCAN_RESULTS to the freed hostapd_data and hostapd crashes in
hostapd_wpa_event(). Seen on a GL-MT3600BE (mt7996e, both bands on one wiphy):
the 5 GHz AP, a later BSS of the phy0 driver, is removed during its HT40 scan
when the uplink station on the same radio reconnects.

---
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -9290,6 +9290,11 @@
 		struct i802_bss *tbss;
 
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: Not the first BSS - remove it");
+		/* A scan this BSS started keeps its timeout armed with bss->ctx,
+		 * which the caller frees once this returns; the first BSS
+		 * branch below cancels its own, this one has to as well. */
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout, drv,
+				     bss->ctx);
 		for (tbss = drv->first_bss; tbss; tbss = tbss->next) {
 			if (tbss->next == bss) {
 				tbss->next = bss->next;
